  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 109,
  "title": "Psalms 109",
  "display_title": "Psalms 109",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 109,
  "sortOrder": 19109,
  "verseCount": 31,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "They compassed me about also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For my love they are my adversaries: but I give myself unto prayer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Let his days be few; and let another take his office.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek their bread also out of their desolate places.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let the strangers spoil his labour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Let there be none to extend mercy unto him: neither let there be any to favour his fatherless children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Let his posterity be cut off; and in the generation following let their name be blotted out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the LORD; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "As he loved cursing, so let it come unto him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Let it be unto him as the garment which covereth him, and for a girdle wherewith he is girded continually.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Let this be the reward of mine adversaries from the LORD, and of them that speak evil against my soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "But do thou for me, O GOD the Lord, for thy name’s sake: because thy mercy is good, deliver thou me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For I am poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "I became also a reproach unto them: when they looked upon me they shaked their heads.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Help me, O LORD my God: O save me according to thy mercy:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "That they may know that this is thy hand; that thou, LORD, hast done it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Let mine adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "I will greatly praise the LORD with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:109:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "For he shall stand at the right hand of the poor, to save him from those that condemn his soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 109:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:109:31"
      }
    }
  ],
